  "check": "R-5",
  "question": "Has the uptake measure been measuring understanding, or just belief movement?",
  "plain_language": "Several experiments measure how much a reader 'takes on' from a work. The measure is a distance between what the reader believed before and after, so a reader who ends up confidently wrong scores almost as highly as one who ends up right: both moved a long way. This splits that one number into three, the important one being how much closer to the truth the reader actually got, which can go negative and which the old measure cannot express.",
